 of the hedrons that once imprisoned the Eldrazi. This coloration is intended to aid deckbuilding and game play.","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Devoid works in all zones, not just on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card loses devoid, it will still be colorless. This is because effects that change an object’s color (like the one created by devoid) are considered before the object loses devoid.","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the player has no cards in their library when the ingest ability resolves, nothing happens. That player won’t lose the game (until they have to draw a card from an empty library).","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Other cards and abilities can give a card with devoid color. If that happens, it’s just the new color, not that color and colorless.","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The card exiled by the ingest ability is exiled face up.","oracle_id":"0767fb65-a621-494b-97a4-f23a4c8b4bec","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
